  "summary": "Malicious code in invest-module-cookie (npm)",
  "details": "Invest-module-cookie@20.8.2 is a multi-platform binary dropper. When required, _adapter.js fingerprints the OS/arch (Windows, macOS, Linux x64, Linux arm64) and downloads a platform-specific binary from Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET to paths like /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. It also uses DNS TXT record exfiltration from c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site as a fallback channel. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe (Windows) and spawned as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"file \u0026\" on Unix). A cooldown file at /tmp/.analytics_state or %TEMP%\\analytics_state prevents re-execution within ~5.7 hours.",
  "affected": [
